{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SdGqgoZW26z4QaKREuLApS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 182,\n3\t \"title\": \"Tray icon missing on GNOME (Wayland) in 44.0.0 / 43.4.1+: StatusNotifierItem registration is rejected\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Electron Version\\n\\n44.0.0 (also 44.0.0-beta.6, 43.4.1, 43.4.2)\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nUbuntu\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nUbuntu 24.04, GNOME with the default ubuntu-appindicators extension, Wayland and Xorg sessions\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\nx64, arm64\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\n44.0.0-beta.5 / 43.4.0 (icon registers; see #52674 for the separate menu problem those had), 42.x fully working\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n`new Tray(image)` registers a StatusNotifierItem with `org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher` and the icon shows in the GNOME top bar.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nNothing is registered with the watcher (`busctl --user get-property org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher /StatusNotifierWatcher org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher RegisteredStatusNotifierItems` never lists the app). On Wayland there is no tray icon at all; on Xorg the legacy XEmbed fallback icon appears instead.\\n\\nThe item calls `RegisterStatusNotifierItem(\\\"org.freedesktop.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-1/StatusNotifierItem/1\\\")`, i.e. the well-known name with the object path appended. GNOME's watcher treats an argument that does not start with `/` as a bus name, `GetNameOwner` fails on that string, and the registration is refused, after which the SNI implementation is torn down. This came in with the cherry-pick of https://crrev.com/c/8250459 in #52951 (44-x-y) and #52952 (43-x-y); upstream fixed it a week later in https://crrev.com/c/8272040 (in Chromium 154.0.8016.0, so `main` already has it), which registers the plain well-known name and exports the item at `/StatusNotifierItem` again.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n```js\\nconst { app, Tray, Menu, nativeImage } = require('electron');\\napp.on('ready', () => {\\n  const t = new Tray(nativeImage.createFromPath('icon.png'));\\n  t.setContextMenu(Menu.buildFromTemplate([{ label: 'Quit', role: 'quit' }]));\\n});\\n```\\n\\nPer-version result against a watcher that resolves items the way the GNOME extension does:\\n\\n| version | RegisterStatusNotifierItem argument | result |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 42.10.0 | `:1.1` | ok |\\n| 43.4.0, 44.0.0-beta.5 | `org.freedesktop.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-1` | registered (menu issue is #52674) |\\n| 43.4.1, 44.0.0-beta.6, 44.0.0 | `org.freedesktop.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-1/StatusNotifierItem/1` | `NameHasNoOwner`, registration refused |\\n\",\n5\t \"labels\": [\n6\t  \"43-x-y\",\n7\t  \"44-x-y\",\n8\t  \"bug :beetle:\",\n9\t  \"platform/linux\"\n10\t ],\n11\t \"state\": \"open\",\n12\t \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n13\t \"as_of\": \"2026-08-26T19:49:32Z\",\n14\t \"replay\": true\n15\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"694747a1-d530-493e-8c52-f584251718f7","uuid":"77b0a649-c2ed-418f-b51b-1562ae8866ba","timestamp":"2026-10-23T12:39:19.441Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/cs467-electron-triage/cs467-electron-triage/.triage/issue.json","content":"{\n \"number\": 182,\n \"title\": \"Tray icon missing on GNOME (Wayland) in 44.0.0 / 43.4.1+: StatusNotifierItem registration is rejected\",\n \"body\": \"### Electron Version\\n\\n44.0.0 (also 44.0.0-beta.6, 43.4.1, 43.4.2)\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nUbuntu\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nUbuntu 24.04, GNOME with the default ubuntu-appindicators extension, Wayland and Xorg sessions\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\nx64, arm64\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\n44.0.0-beta.5 / 43.4.0 (icon registers; see #52674 for the separate menu problem those had), 42.x fully working\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n`new Tray(image)` registers a StatusNotifierItem with `org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher` and the icon shows in the GNOME top bar.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nNothing is registered with the watcher (`busctl --user get-property org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher /StatusNotifierWatcher org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher RegisteredStatusNotifierItems` never lists the app). On Wayland there is no tray icon at all; on Xorg the legacy XEmbed fallback icon appears instead.\\n\\nThe item calls `RegisterStatusNotifierItem(\\\"org.freedesktop.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-1/StatusNotifierItem/1\\\")`, i.e. the well-known name with the object path appended. GNOME's watcher treats an argument that does not start with `/` as a bus name, `GetNameOwner` fails on that string, and the registration is refused, after which the SNI implementation is torn down. This came in with the cherry-pick of https://crrev.com/c/8250459 in #52951 (44-x-y) and #52952 (43-x-y); upstream fixed it a week later in https://crrev.com/c/8272040 (in Chromium 154.0.8016.0, so `main` already has it), which registers the plain well-known name and exports the item at `/StatusNotifierItem` again.\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n```js\\nconst { app, Tray, Menu, nativeImage } = require('electron');\\napp.on('ready', () => {\\n  const t = new Tray(nativeImage.createFromPath('icon.png'));\\n  t.setContextMenu(Menu.buildFromTemplate([{ label: 'Quit', role: 'quit' }]));\\n});\\n```\\n\\nPer-version result against a watcher that resolves items the way the GNOME extension does:\\n\\n| version | RegisterStatusNotifierItem argument | result |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 42.10.0 | `:1.1` | ok |\\n| 43.4.0, 44.0.0-beta.5 | `org.freedesktop.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-1` | registered (menu issue is #52674) |\\n| 43.4.1, 44.0.0-beta.6, 44.0.0 | `org.freedesktop.StatusNotifierItem-<pid>-1/StatusNotifierItem/1` | `NameHasNoOwner`, registration refused |\\n\",\n \"labels\": [\n  \"43-x-y\",\n  \"44-x-y\",\n  \"bug :beetle:\",\n  \"platform/linux\"\n ],\n \"state\": \"open\",\n \"author_association\": \"MEMBER\",\n \"as_of\": \"2026-08-26T19:49:32Z\",\n \"replay\": true\n}","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":15}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SdGqgoZW26z4QaKREuLApS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
